INFANT FOOD MODE (for ~6–12 month old baby):
— Every meal MUST be safe and age-appropriate for a roughly 7-month-old baby.
— Textures: soft, mashable, puréed, or small well-cooked pieces. NO hard, crunchy, or chewy foods.
— NO honey (not even cooked or baked into something — the botulism risk survives cooking). NO added salt. NO added sugar. NO whole nuts or nut pieces. NO raw or undercooked egg. NO cow's milk as a drink (small amounts in cooking are OK). NO unpasteurised dairy. NO high-mercury fish (shark, swordfish, marlin). NO rice drinks.
— NO choking hazards: whole or halved grapes and cherry tomatoes (quarter them lengthways), raw apple or carrot chunks, hot-dog/sausage coins, popcorn, hard candy, whole seeds.
— Smooth nut BUTTER and finely ground nuts are encouraged — early, repeated exposure to common allergens is protective. It is WHOLE nuts and nut pieces that are the choking hazard.
— Prefer: cooked-soft vegetables, iron-rich foods (lentils, well-cooked beans, soft meats, iron-fortified cereals), well-cooked grains, soft fruit.
— Keep preparations simple: 1–3 main ingredients per meal is ideal. Single-ingredient purees are fine.
— Portion sizes should be small and baby-appropriate, not adult portions.
